# Normalize all text to LF in the repo and in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default) checks the tree
# out as CRLF. That is invisible to Windows git, but WSL git -- which reads the
# same worktree with autocrlf unset -- then reports every tracked file as
# modified, and `pull --ff-only` aborts for anyone driving the clone from WSL.
# Shell scripts checked out as CRLF also fail under bash (`bad interpreter`).
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf, so a Windows checkout stays LF too.
# This repo currently contains no binary files; add explicit `binary` rules here
# before committing any (images, audio, archives, fonts).
* text=auto eol=lf
